    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d641">

                <pb facs="0770" n="1604" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1604"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/139</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-04T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 4, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 6, 2.03 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2768. I considered it highly advantageous and urgent in view of my 2765 that the
                    information contained in your 1554 be imparted to the President of the Republic;
                    therefore, acting on discretion allowed me, I imparted to him unofficially on
                    the 3d instant certain portions this telegram. He desired me to assure you that
                    he was touched and thoroughly recognized America’s noble attitude in this
                    matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
